---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import RulerApp from "../components/RulerApp";
---

<Layout>
	<main class="relative w-full min-h-screen bg-canvas dark:bg-ink">
		{/* Ruler App Section */}
		<section class="sticky top-0 w-full h-screen z-10">
			<RulerApp client:only="react" />
		</section>

		{/* SEO Content Section */}
		<section class="relative z-20 bg-canvas dark:bg-ink border-t border-hairline dark:border-white/10 px-6 py-16 md:py-24 max-w-4xl mx-auto shadow-[0_-20px_50px_rgba(0,0,0,0.05)] rounded-t-[40px]">
			<div class="text-ink dark:text-white max-w-none">
				<h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-8 dark:text-white">The Ultimate Online Ruler: Your Accurate Tool for Measuring Anything</h2>
				
				<p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed text-body dark:text-white/80">In today's digital age, having an <strong>online ruler</strong> at your fingertips is essential for designers, engineers, and students alike. Whether you need to measure a physical object against your screen or check dimensions of digital assets, a <strong>free online ruler</strong> provides the convenience you need without searching for a physical measuring tape. Our <strong>accurate online ruler</strong> is designed to be a <strong>real online ruler</strong> that matches physical dimensions perfectly, regardless of your device's screen size.</p>

				<h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-10 mb-4 dark:text-white">Why Use an Online Ruler Inches or CM Tool?</h3>
				<p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed text-body dark:text-white/80">Accuracy is the biggest challenge when using a virtual measurement tool. Most digital rulers fail because they don't account for the Pixel Per Inch (PPI) of your specific display. Our <strong>online ruler tool</strong> solves this by offering multiple calibration methods. Whether you need an <strong>online ruler in cm</strong> for metric projects or an <strong>online ruler inches</strong> tool for imperial measurements, our system ensures that what you see is a <strong>real online ruler</strong> at <strong>actual size</strong>.</p>

				<h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-10 mb-4 dark:text-white">Getting an Actual Size Online Ruler on Every Screen</h3>
				<p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed text-body dark:text-white/80">To achieve an <strong>actual size online ruler</strong>, calibration is key. You can use a standard credit card or enter your screen's diagonal size to get an <strong>online ruler to scale</strong>. This makes our <strong>online ruler inches actual size</strong> feature extremely reliable. If you are working on a 15-inch laptop or a 27-inch monitor, our <strong>accurate online ruler</strong> adjusts its scale so that 1 inch on the screen equals exactly 1 inch in the physical world.</p>

				<h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-10 mb-4 dark:text-white">Metric Measurements: Online Ruler in MM and CM</h3>
				<p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed text-body dark:text-white/80">For those who prefer the metric system, our <strong>online ruler cm</strong> and <strong>online ruler mm</strong> options are perfect. You can toggle between units instantly to get an <strong>online ruler in mm</strong> for high-precision tasks. Having an <strong>mm online ruler</strong> is particularly useful for small electronics parts or detailed craft projects. Our <strong>online ruler in cm</strong> provides a clear, high-contrast display that makes reading measurements effortless.</p>

				<h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-10 mb-4 dark:text-white">Standard Lengths: The 12 Inch Online Ruler</h3>
				<p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed text-body dark:text-white/80">A common requirement for many users is a <strong>12 inch online ruler</strong>. Since 12 inches is the standard length for traditional physical rulers, our <strong>online ruler 12 inch</strong> mode provides that familiar experience. By using our <strong>online ruler actual size</strong> calibration, you can trust that the 12-inch markings on your screen are 100% correct. It’s essentially a digital version of the classic school ruler available on any device.</p>

				<h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-10 mb-4 dark:text-white">Calibrating with an Online Ruler Camera and Devices</h3>
				<p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed text-body dark:text-white/80">While some tools suggest using an <strong>online ruler camera</strong> for calibration, we find that physical reference points like a credit card are more reliable. Our <strong>online ruler tool</strong> works seamlessly across all platforms. Whether you are using a mobile phone or a desktop PC, you can get an <strong>accurate online ruler</strong> in seconds. The flexibility of being a <strong>free online ruler</strong> means you can access professional-grade measurement tools from anywhere in the world.</p>

				<h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-10 mb-4 text-ink dark:text-white">Summary of Key Features</h3>
				<ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-8 space-y-2 text-body dark:text-white/80">
					<li><strong>Online Ruler Inches Actual Size:</strong> Calibrate to ensure physical precision.</li>
					<li><strong>Online Ruler in CM and MM:</strong> Perfect for metric-based engineering and design.</li>
					<li><strong>12 Inch Online Ruler:</strong> The standard length for your daily measuring needs.</li>
					<li><strong>Real Online Ruler:</strong> Avoid the errors of uncalibrated browser-based tools.</li>
					<li><strong>Online Ruler to Scale:</strong> Works on smartphones, tablets, and large monitors.</li>
				</ul>
				
				<p class="mb-12 leading-relaxed text-body dark:text-white/80">In conclusion, when you need a <strong>real online ruler</strong> that you can trust, our <strong>accurate online ruler</strong> is the best choice. Stop guessing and start measuring with confidence using our <strong>online ruler inches</strong> and <strong>online ruler cm</strong> tool today. It is the most versatile <strong>free online ruler</strong> available on the web, built with the modern professional in mind.</p>

				<h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-16 mb-8 dark:text-white">Frequently Asked Questions about Online Rulers</h2>
				
				<div class="space-y-8">
					<div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3 text-ink dark:text-white">Can I use my phone as a ruler?</h3>
						<p class="text-body dark:text-white/80 leading-relaxed">Yes! You can use your phone as a ruler by visiting an <strong>online ruler</strong> website like ours. By calibrating the screen with a standard object like a credit card, your smartphone becomes a highly <strong>accurate online ruler</strong> capable of measuring small objects in <strong>actual size</strong>.</p>
					</div>

					<div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3 text-ink dark:text-white">Is there a ruler online?</h3>
						<p class="text-body dark:text-white/80 leading-relaxed">Yes, there are several <strong>free online ruler</strong> tools available. Our tool is a <strong>real online ruler</strong> that provides <strong>actual size</strong> measurements in both <strong>inches</strong> and <strong>cm</strong> after a quick calibration process.</p>
					</div>

					<div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3 text-ink dark:text-white">How to identify 1 inch?</h3>
						<p class="text-body dark:text-white/80 leading-relaxed">On an <strong>accurate online ruler</strong>, 1 inch is identified by the major numbered markings. If the ruler is properly calibrated to your screen, the physical distance between "0" and "1" will be exactly 25.4mm or one international inch.</p>
					</div>

					<div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3 text-ink dark:text-white">How to measure cm online?</h3>
						<p class="text-body dark:text-white/80 leading-relaxed">To <strong>measure cm online</strong>, simply switch our tool to "cm" mode. Once calibrated, the <strong>online ruler in cm</strong> will show precise metric divisions, where each numbered mark represents one centimeter and the smaller marks represent <strong>mm online ruler</strong> increments.</p>
					</div>

					<div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3 text-ink dark:text-white">Can a smart phone measure?</h3>
						<p class="text-body dark:text-white/80 leading-relaxed">A smartphone can measure physical objects using an <strong>online ruler tool</strong>. Because smartphones have high-density displays, they make for excellent <strong>actual size online rulers</strong> for measuring jewelry, hardware, or small parts.</p>
					</div>

					<div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3 text-ink dark:text-white">Can I use my camera as a ruler?</h3>
						<p class="text-body dark:text-white/80 leading-relaxed">While some apps use an <strong>online ruler camera</strong> feature (AR), they are often less accurate than a screen-based <strong>online ruler to scale</strong>. Using our calibrated screen ruler is generally the most reliable way to get <strong>actual size</strong> results without special hardware.</p>
					</div>

					<div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3 text-ink dark:text-white">Can we measure online?</h3>
						<p class="text-body dark:text-white/80 leading-relaxed">Absolutely. Whether you need to measure digital elements or physical items, you <strong>can measure online</strong> using a browser-based <strong>online ruler inches actual size</strong> tool. It eliminates the need for physical measuring tools in many common scenarios.</p>
					</div>

					<div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3 text-ink dark:text-white">How to read a ruler online?</h3>
						<p class="text-body dark:text-white/80 leading-relaxed">To <strong>read a ruler online</strong>, look for the long lines with numbers for whole units (inches or cm). The medium lines usually represent half-units, and the smallest lines represent <strong>mm</strong> or fractions of an inch (1/16"). Our <strong>online ruler tool</strong> makes this easy with high-contrast markings.</p>
					</div>

					<div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3 text-ink dark:text-white">How to use an online ruler?</h3>
						<p class="text-body dark:text-white/80 leading-relaxed">To <strong>use an online ruler</strong>: 1. Calibrate your screen using a credit card. 2. Select your preferred units (cm/inch). 3. Place your object on the screen or use our measurement tool to click and drag across the area you want to measure.</p>
					</div>

					<div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3 text-ink dark:text-white">How to view or add a ruler in Word/PowerPoint Online?</h3>
						<p class="text-body dark:text-white/80 leading-relaxed">To <strong>show ruler in PowerPoint Online</strong> or <strong>add a ruler in Word Online</strong>, go to the "View" tab in the top ribbon and check the "Ruler" box. If you need to measure something <em>outside</em> of the document area, our <strong>online ruler 12 inch</strong> tool is the perfect companion.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<script type="application/ld+json">
				{
					"@context": "https://schema.org",
					"@type": "FAQPage",
					"mainEntity": [{
						"@type": "Question",
						"name": "Can I use my phone as a ruler?",
						"acceptedAnswer": {
							"@type": "Answer",
							"text": "Yes! You can use your phone as a ruler by visiting a calibrated online ruler website. By using a standard object like a credit card for calibration, your smartphone becomes an accurate measuring tool."
						}
					}, {
						"@type": "Question",
						"name": "Is there a ruler online?",
						"acceptedAnswer": {
							"@type": "Answer",
							"text": "Yes, our free online ruler provides actual size measurements in inches and cm on any device with a web browser."
						}
					}, {
						"@type": "Question",
						"name": "How to identify 1 inch?",
						"acceptedAnswer": {
							"@type": "Answer",
							"text": "On a calibrated online ruler, 1 inch is the distance between the '0' and '1' major markings, representing exactly 25.4mm in physical space."
						}
					}, {
						"@type": "Question",
						"name": "How to measure cm online?",
						"acceptedAnswer": {
							"@type": "Answer",
							"text": "Switch the online ruler tool to 'cm' mode. Once your screen is calibrated, the tool will display precise centimeter and millimeter markings for metric measurement."
						}
					}, {
						"@type": "Question",
						"name": "Can a smart phone measure?",
						"acceptedAnswer": {
							"@type": "Answer",
